<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The private Runtime's Node.js on Intel. Every entitlement here must
	     carry evidence that this process needs it.

	     allow-unsigned-executable-memory: on x86_64, V8 does not allocate its
	     code space with MAP_JIT; it flips ordinary pages to executable. Under
	     the hardened runtime that mprotect fails and Node aborts in
	     v8::base::OS::SetPermissions on its first compiled function, with
	     allow-jit alone too. This entitlement is the minimum that runs
	     JavaScript, WebAssembly, and npm. Apple silicon needs only allow-jit
	     (see runtime-node-aarch64.plist).

	     disable-library-validation: Node loads native addons that npm installs
	     after release, which this Team did not sign. The Show Runtime that
	     renders Show Pages requires rollup, lightningcss, and
	     @tailwindcss/oxide addons that their publishers ship unsigned or
	     ad-hoc signed; with library validation on, each require() fails with
	     "mapping process and mapped file (non-platform) have different Team
	     IDs". Agent backends and their dependencies are installed by npm into
	     the mutable backend root the same way.

	     Deliberately absent: disable-executable-page-protection,
	     allow-dyld-environment-variables, and get-task-allow, which upstream
	     Node's own signature carries. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
